From bdc025b371ae4b9f3d4e7881a9091062b171a348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:29:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] nvidia-x11: unpack the installer through a setup hook

The installer is a Makeself archive, which unpackPhase cannot handle. Add a
setup hook for it and use it for both the userspace libraries and the
proprietary kernel module, so the module is built from the same sources as the
driver it belongs to instead of a separately fetched tree.

Identify the archive by its shell preamble rather than by the file name, so the
Vulkan developer driver, which ships as vulkan-beta-<version>-linux, unpacks
like the rest.

The kernel ceiling is a brokenAbove on the module now, so a driver that builds
while its module does not is marked broken where the failure is.

Assisted-by: omp:Space Bunny Alpha
