From cef019b5879762498907f492a55c00bfb904a15b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:02:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] nvidia-x11: build each driver in a factory and expose
 it as a scope

default.nix is a factory, called once by pkgs and once by linuxPackages. The
first call builds the driver and the userspace tools, the second adds the kernel
modules to the same branch, and a driver can be matched against the modules
built from the same sources. pkgs.nvidiaPackages.production.driver and
pkgs.linuxPackages.nvidiaPackages.production.driver build the same derivation.

nvidiaPackages.<branch> is an attribute set rather than a derivation: .driver
holds the outputs and the tools are siblings. A branch is a
lib.makeExtensible set rather than a scope, because lib.makeScope hands out a
callPackage bound to the scope and taking it forces every member, which would
leave no room for the removed output names below.

The four removed output names warn and hand back .driver.<name> where the branch
builds that output, and say plainly that it does not otherwise. legacy_340 and
legacy_390 have no lib32, and those two plus legacy_470 have no firmware.
Telling the cases apart reads driver.outputs, because ? and lib.hasAttr cannot
be used here: binaries.nix leaves a lib32 attribute behind on the branches that
build no 32-bit libraries, so both report one for legacy_340, whose outputs are
out and bin alone, and reading it overflows the stack.

hardware.nvidia.package is the branch scope, and hardware.nvidia.kernelModules is
the module built for the configured kernel, following package and
hardware.nvidia.open. Its defaultText cannot interpolate config, since the
options documentation is built where config is not available, so it states the
shape and the rule is in the description.

README.md describes the resulting layout.

This commit does not evaluate on its own. The nvidia_x11 aliases here name the
driver, so a consumer that read .settings or .mod off one finds nothing; the
next commit updates them.

Assisted-by: omp:Space Bunny Alpha
