From 365680570ae27e56559b994615f570664936c993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:02:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] nvidia: update the consumers of the driver namespace

hardware.nvidia.package is a branch scope now, and the driver packages live in
pkgs.nvidiaPackages rather than pkgs.linuxPackages.nvidiaPackages. Every
consumer of either has to name the driver it wants instead of using the option
as the package.

The nvidia_x11 aliases in linux-kernels.nix keep working and name the driver of
their branch, so a package that only ever wanted the driver needs no change; the
adjustments here are the ones that read an output, the kernel modules, or a
tools entry off the old shape. The boot.kernelModules example in
system/boot/kernel.nix and the option example in the manual used an alias whose
name no longer describes where the module lives.

Assisted-by: omp:Space Bunny Alpha
